Source adapted from golang.org/x/tools
──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

ken's Go typed tier (internal/gotypes) answers references, implementations
and renames by gopls's own rules, without running gopls. To do that it
contains source adapted from golang.org/x/tools and its gopls module
(gopls v0.23.0):

    internal/gotypes/tsatisfy.go   adapted from refactor/satisfy/find.go
    internal/gotypes/tmsets.go     ports gopls/internal/util/fingerprint and
                                   gopls/internal/cache/methodsets, and the
                                   type matching of
                                   gopls/internal/golang/implementation.go
    internal/gotypes/trefs.go      follows gopls/internal/golang/references.go,
                                   gopls/internal/cache/xrefs and
                                   go/types/objectpath
    internal/gotypes/trename.go    follows gopls/internal/golang/rename.go and
                                   rename_check.go

